,{"id":45,"text":46,"source":47,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":29},"main-page","On the com page itself, `E1` makes the unit visible to bluetooth MIDI hosts and `E3` chooses what the multi-out jack carries.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/com#setting-the-multi-out-port-and-bluetooth-midi",[49],{"id":50,"goal":51,"preconditions":52,"steps":53,"result":23,"source":28,"firmware_min":23,"verified_on":23,"confidence":29},"section","Go to one of the four com sections",[],[54],{"keys":55,"note":56,"set":23},"com → M1…M4","system settings, controller mode, devices or MTP",[],[59,60,61,62,63,64],"com.system-settings","com.controller-mode","com.devices","com.mtp","com.multi-out","com.usb","Think of `com` as the OP-XY's patch bay and system menu in one. The main page itself only holds\nbluetooth MIDI (`E1`) and the multi-out setting (`E3`); everything else is one module key away.\n\nTwo sections change how the unit behaves until you leave them: controller mode turns the panel into\na MIDI controller, and MTP mode takes the USB MIDI connection away while files move.",[67,69,71],{"url":28,"kind":68},"guide",{"url":33,"kind":70},"research",{"url":47,"kind":68},[73,74,75,76,77],"key.com","key.m1","key.m2","key.m3","key.m4",{"id":5,"title":79},"Connectivity",{"id":59,"title":81},"System settings",{"basics.key-notation":83,"basics.main-modes":84,"basics.modules":85,"basics.track-buttons":86,"basics.linked-tracks":87,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":88,"basics.workflow":89,"basics.firmware-versions":90,"hardware.layout":91,"hardware.power-and-charging":92,"hardware.connectors":93,"hardware.specifications":94,"hardware.te-boot":95,"hardware.firmware-update":96,"hardware.factory-reset":97,"hardware.system-menu":98,"hardware.safety-and-care":99,"hardware.in-the-box":100,"sequencer.overview":101,"sequencer.step-entry":102,"sequencer.step-recording":103,"sequencer.live-recording":104,"sequencer.extend-notes":105,"sequencer.nudge":106,"sequencer.single-sound":107,"